<title>FRANCE: Protesters form human chain at French plant site.</title>
<headline>Protesters form human chain at French plant site.</headline>
<dateline>NANTES, France 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Environmentalists formed a human chain about 30 km (19 miles) long on Sunday, the day of a parliamentary election, to protest against plans to build a power station in western France.</p>
<p>The Anti-Nuclear Federation said the chain along the Loire estuary was made up of at least 25,000 people from France, Britain and Germany. The police put the number at 11,000.</p>
<p>State utility Electricite de France (EDF) plans to build a power station, possibly nuclear, at Le Carnet near the city of Nantes.</p>
</text>
